<!--Engine Documentation — Strategies
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation.Strategies-->
<edoc:Strategies xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:edoc="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    How a BlockProcessor selects a strategy
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A BlockProcessor is registered on a RenderTarget for a baseType. Its process
    method calls exactly one engine strategy (or renderTemplates, which is the
    template strategy for many files).

    Compile strategy:

        class ScadBlockProcessor implements BlockProcessor {
          baseType = "com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block"
          process(block, engine) {
            return engine.compile(block, this, context)
          }
        }

    Template strategy:

        class NfcPlayerProcessor implements BlockProcessor {
          baseType = "com.pimachine.nfc.NfcPlayer"
          process(block, engine) {
            return engine.renderTemplates(block, ["nfc_player.py.tpl", "config.json.tpl"])
          }
        }

    Copy strategy:

        class MathBuiltInProcessor implements BlockProcessor {
          baseType = "org.blockml.bml.service.Math"
          process(block, engine) {
            return engine.copyTemplate("lib/math_service.scad", "lib/math_service.scad")
          }
        }

    These class names are illustrative. The SCAD processors are specified by
    @machineblocks/render-target, not by this package. The engine only guarantees
    that each method is available and returns RenderOutput.

    Built-in services (#math, #strings, #numbers, #lists, #bools) are BML in
    @blockml/core (org.blockml.bml.service.*). A target that needs another
    language form registers its own processor and chooses copy or compile.
    Pre-rendered SCAD for those services, when present, lives in
    @machineblocks/core under blocks/org/blockml/bml/service/. That layout is a
    target concern.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="edoc:MixedStrategies" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</edoc:Strategies>
